{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"semantic_review_task|compare_clinical_constructs|proposed_semantic_buckets|unknown|ApprovedSemanticMerge\" /Users/smkzw/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md'","aggregated_output":"596:- when cross-trial comparison is requested, the user requires clinical semantics rather than exact strings or numerically close values: unknown is not the same, and a hard conflict cannot be overridden by a model. The real HTML must use the same scientific view; an internal helper passing while the portal uses the old glossary is not completion. [Task 2]\n606:- `SemanticGroupingProposal` and `semantic_row_digest` bind a proposal to the full observation digest; source changes invalidate it. Use pairwise compatible complete-link buckets to prevent transitive merging; unknown/uncovered observations remain descriptive and are not dropped. A complete clinical unit includes disease/severity, background therapy, population, endpoint/event definition, scale/direction, estimand, denominator, analysis set, statistical form, and actual time window. [Task 2]\n1537:- Reconcile row by row: local PDFs/reviews/labels/protocols may exist while SQLite fields remain `unknown`/`not_found` or protocol/SAP references are blank. Before an HTML rebuild, produce a machine-readable gap inventory keyed by drug/NCT/publication DOI/FDA application/review URL. For CDE, search accepted-product directory by drug, record acceptance number/application type, then search review-task notices by acceptance number. [Task 2]\n1657:- Symptom: endpoint probes show 502/no service or the guard rejects `--task-type benchmark`. Fix: discover the active endpoint (observed later on 8001); use `unknown` only for registration, never as result evidence. [Task 1]\n2409:- Symptom: `init-task --task-type maintenance` fails. Cause: `maintenance` is unsupported by the workflow guard. Fix: use `--task-type unknown --force` only when the maintenance scope has been explicitly authorized. [Task 1]\n3542:- The qualification-AI contract being carried into the frontend was fail-closed: missing standards, duplicate standards, cross IN/EX decisions, unknown evidence, version mismatch, or conflicting evidence should fail the batch rather than write partial AI output, and `needs_medical_confirmation=true` remained a routing marker [Task 5]\n3579:- Symptom: qualification or eligibility AI writes partial or contradictory judgments. Cause: missing standards, duplicate standards, cross IN/EX decisions, unknown evidence, or version mismatch are handled permissively. Fix: keep the batch fail-closed contract, require a human medical reason for decision-like actions, and preserve the UI separation between AI draft and medical judgment [Task 5]\n3677:- The audited architecture is ORCHESTRATOR + L1 multi-source collection + L2 extraction/adjudication + L3 analysis/rendering/QC/export. Its facts rule is: no snapshot, no fact-store entry; unknowns use `null` plus a controlled missing state; restricted sources become `BLOCKED_SOURCE`/evidence debt; insufficient evidence cannot rank; cross-trial comparison must retain non-head-to-head/comparability limits. [Task 3]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
