{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/smkzw/Documents/AI\\\\ Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/.trellis/workflow.md | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Development Workflow\n     2\t\n     3\t---\n     4\t\n     5\t## Core Principles\n     6\t\n     7\t1. **Plan before code** — figure out what to do before you start\n     8\t2. **Specs injected, not remembered** — guidelines are injected via hook/skill, not recalled from memory\n     9\t3. **Persist everything** — research, decisions, and lessons all go to files; conversations get compacted, files don't\n    10\t4. **Incremental development** — one task at a time\n    11\t5. **Capture learnings** — after each task, review and write new knowledge back to spec\n    12\t\n    13\t---\n    14\t\n    15\t## Trellis System\n    16\t\n    17\t### Developer Identity\n    18\t\n    19\tOn first use, initialize your identity:\n    20\t\n    21\t```bash\n    22\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/init_developer.py <your-name>\n    23\t```\n    24\t\n    25\tCreates `.trellis/.developer` (gitignored) + `.trellis/workspace/<your-name>/`.\n    26\t\n    27\t### Spec System\n    28\t\n    29\t`.trellis/spec/` holds coding guidelines organized by package and layer.\n    30\t\n    31\t- `.trellis/spec/<package>/<layer>/index.md` — entry point with **Pre-Development Checklist** + **Quality Check**. Actual guidelines live in the `.md` files it points to.\n    32\t- `.trellis/spec/guides/index.md` — cross-package thinking guides.\n    33\t\n    34\t```bash\n    35\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py --mode packages   # list packages / layers\n    36\t```\n    37\t\n    38\t**When to update spec**: new pattern/convention found · bug-fix prevention to codify · new technical decision.\n    39\t\n    40\t### Task System\n    41\t\n    42\tEvery task has its own directory under `.trellis/tasks/{MM-DD-name}/` holding `task.json`, `prd.md`, optional `design.md`, optional `implement.md`, optional `research/`, and context manifests (`implement.jsonl`, `check.jsonl`) for sub-agent-capable platforms.\n    43\t\n    44\t```bash\n    45\t# Task lifecycle\n    46\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create \"<title>\" [--slug <name>] [--parent <dir>]\n    47\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py start <name>          # set active task (session-scoped when available)\n    48\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py current --source      # show active task and source\n    49\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py finish                # clear active task (triggers after_finish hooks)\n    50\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py archive <name>        # move to archive/{year-month}/\n    51\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py list [--mine] [--status <s>]\n    52\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py list-archive\n    53\t\n    54\t# Code-spec context (injected into implement/check agents via JSONL).\n    55\t# `implement.jsonl` / `check.jsonl` are seeded on `task create` for sub-agent-capable\n    56\t# platforms; the AI curates real spec + research entries during planning when needed.\n    57\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-context <name> <action> <file> <reason>\n    58\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py list-context <name> [action]\n    59\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py validate <name>\n    60\t\n    61\t# Task metadata\n    62\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py set-branch <name> <branch>\n    63\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py set-base-branch <name> <branch>    # PR target\n    64\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py set-scope <name> <scope>\n    65\t\n    66\t# Hierarchy (parent/child)\n    67\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-subtask <parent> <child>\n    68\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py remove-subtask <parent> <child>\n    69\t\n    70\t# PR creation\n    71\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create-pr [name] [--dry-run]\n    72\t```\n    73\t\n    74\t> Run `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py --help` to see the authoritative, up-to-date list.\n    75\t\n    76\t**Current-task mechanism**: `task.py create` creates the task directory and (when session identity is available) auto-sets the per-session active-task pointer so the planning breadcrumb fires immediately. `task.py start` writes the same pointer (idempotent if already set) and flips `task.json.status` from `planning` to `in_progress`. State is stored under `.trellis/.runtime/sessions/`. If no context key is available from hook input, `TRELLIS_CONTEXT_ID`, or a platform-native session environment variable, there is no active task and `task.py start` fails with a session identity hint. `task.py finish` deletes the current session file (status unchanged). `task.py archive <task>` writes `status=completed`, moves the directory to `archive/`, and deletes any runtime session files that still point at the archived task.\n    77\t\n    78\t### Workspace System\n    79\t\n    80\tRecords every AI session for cross-session tracking under `.trellis/workspace/<developer>/`.\n    81\t\n    82\t- `journal-N.md` — session log. **Max 2000 lines per file**; a new `journal-(N+1).md` is auto-created when exceeded.\n    83\t- `index.md` — personal index (total sessions, last active).\n    84\t\n    85\t```bash\n    86\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/add_session.py --title \"Title\" --commit \"hash\" --summary \"Summary\"\n    87\t```\n    88\t\n    89\t### Context Script\n    90\t\n    91\t```bash\n    92\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py                            # full session runtime\n    93\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py --mode packages            # available packages + spec layers\n    94\tpython3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py --mode phase --step <X.Y>  # detailed guide for a workflow step\n    95\t```\n    96\t\n    97\t---\n    98\t\n    99\t<!--\n   100\t  WORKFLOW-STATE BREADCRUMB CONTRACT (read this before editing the tag blocks below)\n   101\t\n   102\t  The [workflow-state:STATUS] blocks embedded in the ## Phase Index section\n   103\t  below are the SINGLE source of truth for the per-turn `<workflow-state>`\n   104\t  breadcrumb that every supported AI platform's UserPromptSubmit hook\n   105\t  reads. inject-workflow-state.py (Python platforms) and\n   106\t  inject-workflow-state.js (OpenCode plugin) only parse them — there is no\n   107\t  fallback dict baked into the scripts after v0.5.0-rc.0.\n   108\t\n   109\t  STATUS charset: [A-Za-z0-9_-]+. When the hook can't find a tag, it\n   110\t  degrades to a generic \"Refer to workflow.md for current step.\" line —\n   111\t  intentionally visible so users notice and fix a broken workflow.md.\n   112\t\n   113\t  INVARIANT (test/regression.test.ts):\n   114\t    Every workflow-walkthrough step marked `[required · once]` must have a\n   115\t    matching enforcement line in its phase's [workflow-state:*] block. The\n   116\t    breadcrumb is the only per-turn channel; if a mandatory step isn't\n   117\t    mentioned there, the AI silently skips it (Phase 1 planning gate\n   118\t    skip and Phase 3.4 commit skip both manifested via this gap).\n   119\t\n   120\t  TAG ↔ PHASE scoping:\n   121\t    [workflow-state:no_task]      → no active task; before Phase 1\n   122\t    [workflow-state:planning]     → all of Phase 1 (status='planning')\n   123\t    [workflow-state:planning-inline] → Codex inline variant of Phase 1\n   124\t    [workflow-state:in_progress]  → Phase 2 + Phase 3.2-3.4\n   125\t                                    (status stays 'in_progress' from\n   126\t                                    task.py start until task.py archive)\n   127\t    [workflow-state:in_progress-inline] → Codex inline variant of Phase 2/3\n   128\t    [workflow-state:completed]    → currently DEAD: cmd_archive flips\n   129\t                                    status and moves the dir in the same\n   130\t                                    call, so the resolver loses the\n   131\t                                    pointer (block kept for a future\n   132\t                                    explicit in_progress→completed\n   133\t                                    transition)\n   134\t\n   135\t  Editing checklist:\n   136\t    - When you change a [workflow-state:STATUS] block, also check the\n   137\t      matching phase's `[required · once]` walkthrough steps for sync\n   138\t    - Run `trellis update` after editing to push the new bodies to\n   139\t      downstream user projects (block-level managed replacement)\n   140\t    - Full runtime contract:\n   141\t      .trellis/spec/cli/backend/workflow-state-contract.md\n   142\t-->\n   143\t\n   144\t## Phase Index\n   145\t\n   146\t```\n   147\tPhase 1: Plan    → classify, get task-creation consent, then write planning artifacts\n   148\tPhase 2: Execute → implement only after task status is in_progress\n   149\tPhase 3: Finish  → verify, update spec, commit, and wrap up\n   150\t```\n   151\t\n   152\t### Request Triage\n   153\t\n   154\t- Simple conversation or small task: ask only whether this turn should create a Trellis task. If the user says no, skip Trellis for this session.\n   155\t- Complex task: ask whether you may create a Trellis task and enter planning. If the user says no, do not do broad inline implementation; explain, clarify scope, or suggest a smaller split.\n   156\t- User approval to create a task is not approval to start implementation. Planning still happens first.\n   157\t\n   158\t### Planning Artifacts\n   159\t\n   160\t- `prd.md` — requirements, constraints, and acceptance criteria. Do not put technical design or execution checklists here.\n   161\t- `design.md` — technical design for complex tasks: boundaries, contracts, data flow, tradeoffs, compatibility, rollout / rollback shape.\n   162\t- `implement.md` — execution plan for complex tasks: ordered checklist, validation commands, review gates, and rollback points.\n   163\t- `implement.jsonl` / `check.jsonl` — spec and research manifests for sub-agent context. They do not replace `implement.md`.\n   164\t- Lightweight tasks may be PRD-only. Complex tasks must have `prd.md`, `design.md`, and `implement.md` before `task.py start`.\n   165\t\n   166\t### Parent / Child Task Trees\n   167\t\n   168\tUse a parent task when one user request contains several independently verifiable deliverables. The parent task owns the source requirement set, the task map, cross-child acceptance criteria, and final integration review; it normally should not be the implementation target unless it also has direct work.\n   169\t\n   170\tUse child tasks for deliverables that can be planned, implemented, checked, and archived independently. Parent/child structure is not a dependency system: if one child must wait for another, write that ordering in the child `prd.md` / `implement.md` and keep each child's acceptance criteria testable.\n   171\t\n   172\tCreate new children with `task.py create \"<title>\" --slug <name> --parent <parent-dir>`. Link existing tasks with `task.py add-subtask <parent> <child>`, and unlink mistakes with `task.py remove-subtask <parent> <child>`.\n   173\t\n   174\t<!-- Per-turn breadcrumb: shown when there is no active task (before Phase 1) -->\n   175\t\n   176\t[workflow-state:no_task]\n   177\tNo active task. First classify the current turn and ask for task-creation consent before creating any Trellis task.\n   178\tSimple conversation / small task: ask only whether this turn should create a Trellis task. If the user says no, skip Trellis for this session.\n   179\tComplex task: ask the user if you can create a Trellis task and enter the planning phase. If the user says no, explain, clarify scope, or suggest a smaller split.\n   180\t[/workflow-state:no_task]\n   181\t\n   182\t### Phase 1: Plan\n   183\t- 1.0 Create task `[required · once]` (only after task-creation consent)\n   184\t- 1.1 Requirement exploration `[required · repeatable]` (`prd.md`; complex tasks also need `design.md` + `implement.md`)\n   185\t- 1.2 Research `[optional · repeatable]`\n   186\t- 1.3 Configure context `[required · once]` — Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode, Codex, Kiro, Gemini, Qoder, CodeBuddy, Copilot, Droid, Pi, Oh My Pi, ZCode, Snow, Reasonix, Grok, Kimi Code (sub-agent-dispatch platforms only; inline platforms skip)\n   187\t- 1.4 Activate task `[required · once]` (review gate, then `task.py start`; status → in_progress)\n   188\t- 1.5 Completion criteria\n   189\t\n   190\t<!-- Per-turn breadcrumb: shown throughout Phase 1 (status='planning') -->\n   191\t\n   192\t[workflow-state:planning]\n   193\tLoad `trellis-brainstorm`; stay in planning.\n   194\tLightweight: `prd.md` can be enough. Complex: finish `prd.md`, `design.md`, and `implement.md`; ask for review before `task.py start`.\n   195\tMulti-deliverable scope: consider a parent task plus independently verifiable child tasks; dependencies must be written in child artifacts, not implied by tree position.\n   196\tSub-agent mode: curate `implement.jsonl` and `check.jsonl` as spec/research manifests before start.\n   197\t[/workflow-state:planning]\n   198\t\n   199\t<!-- Per-turn breadcrumb: shown throughout Phase 1 when codex.dispatch_mode=inline.\n   200\t     Codex-only opt-in alternate to [workflow-state:planning]. The main agent\n   201\t     edits code directly in Phase 2, so jsonl curation is skipped —\n   202\t     the inline workflow loads `trellis-before-dev` instead of injecting JSONL\n   203\t     into a sub-agent. -->\n   204\t\n   205\t[workflow-state:planning-inline]\n   206\tLoad `trellis-brainstorm`; stay in planning.\n   207\tLightweight: `prd.md` can be enough. Complex: finish `prd.md`, `design.md`, and `implement.md`; ask for review before `task.py start`.\n   208\tMulti-deliverable scope: consider a parent task plus independently verifiable child tasks; dependencies must be written in child artifacts, not implied by tree position.\n   209\tInline mode: skip jsonl curation; Phase 2 reads artifacts/specs via `trellis-before-dev`.\n   210\t[/workflow-state:planning-inline]\n   211\t\n   212\t### Phase 2: Execute\n   213\t- 2.1 Implement `[required · repeatable]`\n   214\t- 2.2 Quality check `[required · repeatable]`\n   215\t- 2.3 Rollback `[on demand]`\n   216\t\n   217\t<!-- Per-turn breadcrumb: shown while status='in_progress'.\n   218\t     Scope: all of Phase 2 + Phase 3.2-3.4 (status stays 'in_progress' from\n   219\t     task.py start until task.py archive; only archive flips it). The body\n   220\t     therefore must cover every required step from implementation through\n   221\t     commit, including Phase 3.3 spec update and Phase 3.4 commit. -->\n   222\t\n   223\tSub-agent dispatch protocol applies to all platforms and all sub-agents, including native Codex `SubagentStart` context injection with child-side pull fallback, class-2 Gemini/Qoder/Copilot/Reasonix/Trae/Grok/Kimi Code, hook-backed ZCode/Snow, and `trellis-research`: every dispatch prompt starts with `Active task: <task path from task.py current>` before role-specific instructions. On Grok Build, use `spawn_subagent` with `subagent_type` set to the Trellis agent name (e.g. `trellis-implement`). On Kimi Code, dispatch the built-in `coder` / `explore` sub-agent with the matching `.kimi-code/skills/trellis-<role>/SKILL.md` instructions.\n   224\t\n   225\t[workflow-state:in_progress]\n   226\tTools: `trellis-implement` / `trellis-research` are sub-agent types only (Task/Agent tool, NOT Skill; there is no skill by these names). `trellis-update-spec` is a skill. `trellis-check` exists as both; prefer the Agent form when verifying after code changes.\n   227\tFlow: `trellis-implement` -> `trellis-check` -> `trellis-update-spec` -> commit (Phase 3.4) -> `/trellis:finish-work`.\n   228\tMain-session default: dispatch implement/check sub-agents. Sub-agent self-exemption: if already running as `trellis-implement`, do NOT spawn another `trellis-implement` or `trellis-check`; if already running as `trellis-check`, do NOT spawn another `trellis-check` or `trellis-implement`. Dispatch is main session only.\n   229\tDispatch prompt starts with `Active task: <task path from task.py current>`. Read context: jsonl entries -> `prd.md` -> `design.md if present` -> `implement.md if present`.\n   230\t[/workflow-state:in_progress]\n   231\t\n   232\t<!-- Per-turn breadcrumb: shown while status='in_progress' when\n   233\t     codex.dispatch_mode=inline. Codex-only opt-in alternate to\n   234\t     [workflow-state:in_progress]. The main session edits code directly\n   235\t     instead of dispatching sub-agents. -->\n   236\t\n   237\t[workflow-state:in_progress-inline]\n   238\tFlow: `trellis-before-dev` -> edit -> `trellis-check` -> validation -> `trellis-update-spec` -> commit (Phase 3.4) -> `/trellis:finish-work`.\n   239\tDo not dispatch implement/check sub-agents in inline mode.\n   240\tRead context: `prd.md` -> `design.md if present` -> `implement.md if present`, plus relevant spec/research loaded by skills.\n   241\t[/workflow-state:in_progress-inline]\n   242\t\n   243\t### Phase 3: Finish\n   244\t- 3.2 Debug retrospective `[on demand]`\n   245\t- 3.3 Spec update `[required · once]`\n   246\t- 3.4 Commit changes `[required · once]`\n   247\t- 3.5 Wrap-up reminder\n   248\t\n   249\t> Note: step 3.1 was folded into 2.2 (last-iteration full-scope check) and 3.4 (commit preamble). Numbering kept stable to avoid breaking external references.\n   250\t\n   251\t<!-- Per-turn breadcrumb: shown while status='completed'.\n   252\t     Currently DEAD in normal flow: cmd_archive writes status='completed' in\n   253\t     the same call that moves the task dir to archive/, so the active-task\n   254\t     resolver loses the pointer and the hook never fires on archived tasks.\n   255\t     Block preserved for a future status-transition redesign (e.g. an\n   256\t     explicit in_progress→completed command). Edit through the same spec\n   257\t     channel as the live blocks. -->\n   258\t\n   259\t[workflow-state:completed]\n   260\tCode committed. Run `/trellis:finish-work`; if dirty, return to Phase 3.4 first.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 3 \"语义|semantic|48|50|时间窗|独立复核|工作项\" docs/specs/competitive-intelligence-workflow-design-v1.3.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 3 \"语义|semantic|48|50|时间窗|独立复核|工作项\" docs/specs/competitive-intelligence-workflow-design-v1.3.md'","aggregated_output":"19-系统是面向医学经理和医学总监的、可审计的科学事实与证据产品，不是一次性搜索脚本、提示词串联器或通用 AI 仪表盘。产品由以下部分组成：\n20-\n21-1. 一个可安装、可版本化的 Skill 包和一个公开入口 Skill；\n22:2. 多个具有稳定输入、输出、错误和恢复语义的内部 Skill；\n23-3. 一个由应用持有的类型化控制图和一个本地确定性执行器；\n24-4. 每项目自包含的证据、事实、快照、运行记录和报告目录；\n25-5. 三个独立的高密度多页面 HTML 门户：A、B、C；\n--\n133-宿主 Agent 的自主研究和用户提供的 typed package 走同一校验、身份、门槛和快照路径；不得因输入方式不同而放宽来源权重、缺失状态、冲突规则或独立审查。研究包中的候选值不是已接受事实，必须经过确定性规范化和科学 QC。\n134-\n135-产品交接采用双层但单一信任边界：通用 v1.3 审计信封记录来源、路由、闭包、\n136:恢复和独立复核，并以规范路径和 SHA-256 绑定每个所选 A/B/C 专属科学载荷；\n137-确定性引擎只有在提交 manifest、信封和载荷当前字节全部复核通过后才能运行。\n138-松散 `report-data.json`、未绑定的 A/B/C 载荷、聊天文本或手写完成状态不能成为\n139-产品输入。该双层结构不是两个科学真源：信封负责跨报告审计闭包，专属载荷负责\n--\n372-\n373-B 核心比较层纳入目标适应症中有结果的 II/III 期、关键或注册相关试验；特殊早期试验只有明确的罕见病、肿瘤或加速开发决策证据角色才可进入特殊核心。早期、延伸、亚组、事后和真实世界研究保留支持层及理由，默认排除研究不得被隐式混入。\n374-\n375:每项核心结果试验至少覆盖：试验身份/阶段/角色；目标人群、队列/组别、治疗和对照；组别基线样本量、年龄、性别及适应症严重程度锚点；至少一个核心疗效终点原始定义、方向、单位、评估时间、分析人群、治疗组、对照组和分母；可直接支持或确定性复算的效应；至少一个 TEAE 或 SAE 数值记录及定义、时间窗、组别和分母；来源角色、披露成熟度和精确定位。\n376-\n377-基线门槛按每个可比较研究组判断，多臂试验不能用合并总体值伪装组别覆盖。均值/中位数、年龄分箱、性别分类、疾病量表版本、方向、单位和基线时间不兼容时必须分面或拆成小多图，不得估算、补造类别或以总体值替代。试验完成/处置字段全部建模但非阻断；未公开、来源未列示、技术不可用、不适用和明确为 0 必须分开。\n378-\n379-### 8.2 整体临床构念分组\n380-\n381:B 的终点和时间窗分组采用“模型辅助的整体临床构念语义分组 + 确定性冲突守卫”：模型可以提出同一临床构念、方向和分析语境的候选组，但不能单独改变组。48 周与 50 周等接近时间窗，在兼容的构念、定义、方向、单位、估计目标、分母和分析集下可以共用一个比较框，并在图题或标记中明确实际时间差；它们不是无差别合并。\n382-\n383-以下任一项不兼容时必须拆分为独立小多图/表：量表或仪器、定义、方向、单位、估计目标、分母、分析集、分析形式或实质不同的时间语境。没有版本化兼容规则时，不能由模型临场合并。治疗组、对照组、原始终点角色、原始值、差异标签和证据入口始终保留。\n384-\n--\n388-\n389-B 至少包含：首页、疗效、纵向结果、安全性、基线与人群、试验完成情况、试验/暴露语境、亚组与支持证据、产品/试验档案、疗效—安全性矩阵、证据与局限。结构化的疗效、纵向、AE、基线和处置数据均先图后表；每张图后提供同一过滤 row set 的完整折叠表。\n390-\n391:B 的气泡图使用版本化临床预设组，不能由模型临场发明坐标轴：①疗效信号 × 总体安全性，大小为治疗组样本量或暴露量；②疗效信号 × 严重风险，大小为有效分析集规模；③获益持续性 × 停药风险，大小为长期暴露量。只有人群、终点/事件、方向、时间窗、估计目标、分析集和分母构成的完整临床语义基本可比时才进入同一图；不兼容内容进入相邻小多图。原始数值、方向、实际时间窗、分析集和分母在同模块折叠表中完整保留。\n392-\n393-安全性热图至少覆盖 TEAE、SAE、AESI、常见 TEAE 和发生率；有数据时加入死亡、3 级及以上 AE、导致停药 AE 和治疗相关 TEAE。颜色只在相同事件和可比语境内表达高低；数值印在单元格，缺失/未报告/低于阈值/技术不可用/明确为 0 用不同状态。图例、对照语境、分母和缺失状态说明必须可见；不得输出雷达图或证据成熟度矩阵。\n394-\n--\n406-\n407-C 页面至少包含：设计首页、设计图谱、试验档案、人群与疾病定义、入选标准、排除标准、分组/干预/对照、终点—定义—时间点矩阵、访视/疗程/随访/延伸、样本量/分析集/公开统计设计、设计模式/异常点/权衡/多路径综合、证据版本与局限。只输入适应症的验收必须形成至少两条有来源依据的候选设计路径，或明确缺少产品特异背景而不作唯一建议。\n408-\n409:C 的主要图形至少覆盖与数据适配的设计模式地图、试验时间轴、终点—时间窗矩阵、入排主题分布、组别结构和方案差异图；完整入排条目、终点定义和方案参数保留在同模块折叠表中。多路径是证据支持的选项空间，不是自动生成唯一“最佳方案”。\n410-\n411----\n412-\n--\n428-\n429-页面级筛选包括适应症、产品、靶点/机制和试验；模块级筛选包括终点、时间点、效应形式、分析人群、AE、设计要素、量表，以及 B 的队列/组别、变量域/字段族、统计形式、原因、分母角色、计量对象、披露状态。页面和模块状态分别写入网址；无数据模块显示限制范围和准确空状态，不自行扩大筛选。\n430-\n431:点击图、表格、时间线或矩阵单元格，可以在原页面打开证据下钻并保持筛选、滚动和焦点。下钻显示产品、试验、组别、终点/事件/设计要素、量表、时间、值/阈值/单位、分子/分母、来源版本和精确登记字段/页/表/段定位；对基线和处置事实显示统计形式、计量对象、分母角色、原因语义、互斥/穷尽和差异标签。下钻可显示原文和规范化说明，但原文永远保留；其存在不能替代完整折叠表和页底来源区。\n432-\n433-每页底部仅设置一个聚合的外部来源区，面向用户显示可访问的来源标题、来源类型、发布日期、数据截止日、链接和简洁限制。用户可见表格不得出现仓库相对路径、绝对路径、内部 receipt、run/job/session ID、门槛计算、源文件定位字段或搜索重试日志。完整路由与诊断留在项目证据和日志。\n434-\n--\n472-\n473-HTML 中的事实、图点、矩阵单元和声明可以导出修订建议，但不能直接编辑科学真源。建议经过来源、身份、上下文、冲突和影响集核验，进入 `validated_pending_user_approval`；只有用户明确批准后才能建立新版本并局部重建。拒绝或证据不足追加记录，不改变当前快照。\n474-\n475:刷新是用户手动触发、随后全自动完成的增量能力：从最近接受快照、来源回执和缺口账本重新核验可变事实，复核新增变化、异常数量和历史集合差异，生成新来源/事实/声明/HTML 版本，保存新增、变化、撤回、取代和未变化 diff，只重算受影响页面。v1 不建设定时监测 Skill、不在无人触发时轮询来源，也不自动发布未经门槛与独立复核接受的报告。移除监测能力不影响打开、恢复和用户触发的自动刷新链。\n476-\n477----\n478-\n--\n503-\n504-### 13.3 验收层级\n505-\n506:必须覆盖包完整性、schema/状态/稳定 ID、来源回执和研究包、宇宙关闭与两轮恢复、A/B/C 门槛、语义兼容和无池化、HTML 页面/搜索/导航/筛选/网址/表格/证据下钻/无障碍、三宿主、用户触发的自动刷新链/历史、恢复包、秘密/绝对路径/远程依赖和 24 门户真实来源矩阵。确定性检查和真实 Chromium/WebKit 渲染缺一不可。\n507-\n508:关键负向矩阵至少覆盖：拥挤领域初搜只发现少数竞品；网络错误被误判为真实无数据；Yaozh 无账号或会话失效；必需论文无法下载且用户确认无法取得；48/50 周可近似归并但不同量表、方向、估计目标、分母或分析集不得误合并；无可绘制数据时不得出现空坐标轴；重名/错误/扫描 publication 或登记号不一致；刷新后的新增、修订和撤回事实/来源进入正确差异；宿主无法创建独立上下文时预检失败且不得主 Agent 自证。\n509-\n510----\n511-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
